            <ArticleTitle>Bronchial asthma induced by an antithyroid drug.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1598-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report the case of a 67-year-old woman who suffered from a severe asthma exacerbation as a consequence of an antithyroid drug treatment prescribed for her multinodular, hyperfunctioning goiter. Asthma symptoms were associated with a very significant increase in the number of eosinophils, detected in both blood and induced sputum.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
